{"id": "produce-market-director-tenant-rents", "title": "At the City’s wholesale produce market, directors’ companies rent space", "seconds": 49.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "tempo": 1.106, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "4545ca723821d11d", "words": 148, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Three businesses owned by sitting directors rented space from the produce market operator.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.23, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["Who", "rented", "space", "at", "the", "market?"], "sub": "2024 disclosures"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.75, 0.98, 1.15, 1.46, 1.89, 2.18, 2.53, 2.72, 2.82, 3.24, 3.55]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The operator reported 568,945 dollars from those three transactions in 2024.", "t0": 4.35, "t1": 11.21, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "irs2024", "kicker": "Internal Revenue Service", "text": "2024 return", "mark": "2024 return"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.61, 1.05, 1.37, 1.65, 2.13, 3.06, 3.28, 3.51, 3.95, 4.34, 4.5, 4.69, 4.92, 5.59, 5.72, 6.01]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Whether the tenants received special terms is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 11.33, "t1": 14.6, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Terms of the subleases"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.37, 0.75, 1.14, 1.51, 1.83, 1.96, 2.03, 2.58, 2.78, 2.85]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The payments went from tenants to the operator.", "t0": 14.72, "t1": 16.79, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Three disclosed rental transactions", "heading": "Rent in 2024", "source": "irs2024", "rows": [{"icon": "lease", "label": "First transaction", "value": "$240,739"}, {"icon": "lease", "label": "Second transaction", "value": "$187,585"}, {"icon": "lease", "label": "Third transaction", "value": "$140,621"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.46, 0.64, 0.82, 1.19, 1.31, 1.44]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "The operator disclosed director-related rents each year from 2020 through 2024.", "t0": 16.91, "t1": 21.67, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "irs2020", "kicker": "Internal Revenue Service", "text": "2020 return", "mark": "2020 return"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.61, 1.04, 1.74, 1.99, 2.21, 2.47, 2.66, 3.02, 3.68, 3.95, 4.21]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "One amount also appeared under a former director. Adding both entries could count it twice.", "t0": 21.79, "t1": 26.75, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$140,621", "label": "Also listed under a former director"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.42, 0.71, 1.06, 1.26, 1.34, 1.62, 2.75, 3.09, 3.36, 3.75, 3.92, 4.17, 4.28]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "The 2022 lease required an annual statement of dealings with board members.", "t0": 26.97, "t1": 31.04, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "lease22", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors", "text": "Section 8.3", "mark": "Section 8.3"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.43, 0.89, 1.32, 1.8, 1.93, 2.29, 2.63, 2.72, 3.05, 3.21, 3.45]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "For rents below 90 percent of the schedule, the lease sets out a City review process.", "t0": 31.16, "t1": 35.5, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "90% of scheduled market rent"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.45, 0.75, 1.0, 1.29, 1.36, 1.44, 2.32, 2.48, 2.67, 2.93, 3.11, 3.2, 3.48, 3.76]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "City staff described an exchange: net proceeds would go back into the market.", "t0": 35.62, "t1": 39.8, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "staff", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors", "text": "Market reinvestment", "mark": "Market reinvestment"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.68, 1.12, 1.23, 2.38, 2.61, 3.1, 3.25, 3.38, 3.59, 3.78, 3.87]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "The Board’s 2026 authorization retained market-rent oversight.", "t0": 39.92, "t1": 43.37, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "board", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors", "text": "2026 authorization", "mark": "2026 authorization"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.43, 0.77, 1.29, 1.99, 2.41, 2.91]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "next[0]"], "text": "The subleases and comparable rents would show how the terms compared.", "t0": 43.49, "t1": 46.83, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Subleases", "Comparable rents"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.76, 0.91, 1.35, 1.58, 1.74, 2.01, 2.13, 2.24, 2.55]}, {"scene": "lease", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 46.95, "t1": 48.74, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.35, 0.44, 0.53, 0.92, 1.07, 1.17]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Who rented space?", "lease": "What the City required"}, "look": "midnight", "hook": "person"}